WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:09.090
It is widely accepted that an important goal of education is to help students learn how to learn.
人们普遍认为，教育的一个重要目标是帮助学生学会如何学习。

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:16.410
In a world where knowledge keeps growing and changing, no school can teach students everything they will need in the future.
在一个知识不断增长和变化的世界里，没有哪所学校能把学生将来需要的一切都教给他们。

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:28.950
Learning how to learn means mastering the skills that make lifelong learning possible: setting goals, finding and evaluating information, managing time and reflecting on one’s own progress.
学会如何学习，意味着掌握那些让终身学习成为可能的技能：设定目标、查找并评估信息、管理时间，以及反思自己的进步。

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:34.570
Students who have these skills can teach themselves new subjects long after they leave school.
掌握了这些技能的学生，在离开学校很久以后，仍然能够自学新的学科。

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:43.200
By contrast, those who are used to memorizing whatever their teachers tell them may feel helpless when facing unfamiliar problems.
相比之下，那些习惯于把老师讲的东西统统背下来的学生，在面对陌生的问题时可能会束手无策。

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.990
As the saying goes, “Give a man a fish and you feed him for a day; teach him to fish and you feed him for a lifetime.”
俗话说：“给人一条鱼，你只能供他吃一天；教他钓鱼，你就能供他吃一辈子。”

00:00:51.790 --> 00:01:01.820
To achieve this goal, teachers should shift from simply delivering knowledge to guiding students as they explore it, for example through projects, discussions and research tasks.
为了实现这一目标，教师应当从单纯地传授知识，转向在学生探索知识时加以引导，比如通过项目、讨论和研究任务来进行。

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:08.260
Schools can also teach study skills directly, such as how to take notes and review effectively.
学校也可以直接教授学习技能，比如如何记笔记、如何有效地复习。

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:12.910
Students, in turn, should take an active role in their own learning.
而学生则应当在自己的学习中发挥积极主动的作用。

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:17.020
Once they know how to learn, they will never stop growing.
一旦他们懂得了如何学习，就永远不会停止成长。
